  "tagline": "Fujitsu BS2000 mainframe DBMS combining a CODASYL network model with SQL on the same data.",
  "description": "UDS/SQL is the CODASYL-style database system for Fujitsu's BS2000 mainframe operating system, originally introduced by Siemens as UDS in 1976. Data is designed as network-model record types and sets, but the same data can also be queried relationally: programs use COBOL DML or CALL DML, and ISO SQL is available alongside. It integrates with the openUTM transaction monitor, and the UDS-D add-on processes data across BS2000 networks with distributed transactions. Fujitsu still develops it: V2.9B (November 2024) added features such as CSV bulk loading, and V2.9C manuals were published in 2026.",
